{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CduR6ohSu5KHHCvW2fLsY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Triage Disposition\n\n1. **Severity: CRITICAL** — Confirm as written. This bypasses release gating on the actual deployment platform (macOS bash 3.2), allowing broken releases through.\n\n2. **Root cause clarification**: Associative arrays silently fail in bash 3.2 — the `declare -A` succeeds but subsequent `${seen_gates[$name]}` lookups return empty, causing gate checks to pass vacuously.\n\n3. **Before relaying to team:**\n   - Verify the deploy README confirms macOS-only execution path (you've already seen this)\n   - Spot-check if `set -e` or `set -u` would catch the failure (likely not — empty variable expansion isn't an error)\n   - Confirm no existing bash version guard or `.bash_version` requirement file exists\n\n4. **Relay with:**\n   - Severity: **CRITICAL**\n   - Exact wording: \"Associative array syntax fails silently on macOS bash 3.2 (deployment platform), causing gate validations to be skipped and releasing broken builds.\"\n   - Recommendation: Replace associative array with compatible alternative (e.g., `grep`-based lookup in a flat list, or `case` statement) OR enforce bash ≥4.0 requirement in deploy setup.\n\n5. **Don't merge** — this is a genuine security/reliability gap on the live deployment target."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":311,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":327,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
